// Phase 2 execution baseline: the dogfood stress-batch PaaS re-platforming
// plan (session 8, first-pass clean at 18 phases / 11 verified loops),
// extended to cover every DSL v0 construct plus the execution metadata that
// Phase 2 ingests: external refs (github/jira/linear/url) and delivery config.
// The conformance suite (spec/conformance) walks this plan end to end.
# project: paas-replatform
# github:repo: acme/platform
# jira:site: https://acme.atlassian.net
# linear:workspace: acme
# ref: https://wiki.acme.dev/replatform-brief
# delivery: single-branch
# report: per-phase

VAR auth_cutbacks = 0
VAR billing_cutbacks = 0
VAR respin_budget = 6
VAR freeze_window = "unbooked"
VAR observability_live = false
VAR approach = "strangler"

-> observability_build

=== observability_build ===
Build the new observability stack: metrics, logs, traces, dashboards and alerting on the PaaS.
Nothing else ships until this is live; without it we fly blind.
# github:issue: 21
# linear: OBS-104
* [Stack live, dashboards and alerts verified] -> auth_extraction

=== auth_extraction ===
Extract the auth service from the monolith behind a strangler-fig facade.
Done means the new service can take auth calls in shadow while the monolith stays authoritative.
# github:issue: 22
# delivery: pr-per-phase
# delivery:branch: replatform/{phase}
~ observability_live = true
+ {approach == "strangler"} [Extraction complete, start shadowing] -> auth_shadow

=== auth_shadow ===
Mirror production auth traffic to the new service and compare results.
Parity metrics must hold for two full weeks before cutover is considered.
+ [Parity metrics held for two weeks] -> auth_capacity_signoff
+ [Parity drifting, rework the extraction] ~loop~ -> auth_extraction

=== auth_capacity_signoff ===
Platform SRE reviews capacity ahead of the auth cutover.
# jira: SRE-311
+ [SRE signs off capacity] @human -> auth_cutover
+ [SRE flags gaps, remediate and re-shadow] @human ~loop~ -> auth_shadow

=== auth_cutover ===
Cut live auth traffic over to the new service and watch the error budget for one week.
Burning more than 20 percent of the error budget in week one triggers a cutback.
+ [Week-one burn within error budget] -> billing_extraction
+ [Burned over 20 percent of error budget, cut back] -> auth_cutback_fix

=== auth_cutback_fix ===
Auth traffic is cut back to the monolith while the team fixes the regression.
# critical-path
~ auth_cutbacks += 1
~ respin_budget -= 1
+ {auth_cutbacks < 3} [Fixed, re-run shadow parity] ~loop~ -> auth_shadow
+ {auth_cutbacks >= 3} [Third cutback, auth approach goes to the architecture board] @human -> arch_board_review

=== billing_extraction ===
Extract the billing service from the monolith behind a strangler-fig facade.
Done means shadow ledger entries are being written alongside the monolith ledger.
# github:issue: 23
# delivery: pr-per-phase
# delivery:branch: replatform/{phase}
+ [Extraction complete, start shadowing] -> billing_shadow

=== billing_shadow ===
Mirror production billing traffic, writing shadow ledger entries, and compare results.
Parity metrics must hold for two full weeks before reconciliation begins.
+ [Parity metrics held for two weeks] -> billing_reconciliation
+ [Parity drifting, rework the extraction] ~loop~ -> billing_extraction

=== billing_reconciliation ===
Finance reconciles a full month of shadow ledger entries against the monolith ledger, to the penny.
Billing cannot cut over until this reconciliation passes.
# jira: FIN-208
+ [Finance confirms the month reconciles to the penny] @human -> billing_capacity_signoff
+ [Discrepancies found, fix and re-run a ledger month] @human ~loop~ -> billing_shadow

=== billing_capacity_signoff ===
Platform SRE reviews capacity ahead of the billing cutover.
+ [SRE signs off capacity] @human -> billing_cutover
+ [SRE flags gaps, remediate and re-shadow] @human ~loop~ -> billing_shadow

=== billing_cutover ===
Cut live billing traffic over to the new service and watch the error budget for one week.
Burning more than 20 percent of the error budget in week one triggers a cutback.
+ [Week-one burn within error budget] -> monolith_freeze_booking
+ [Burned over 20 percent of error budget, cut back] -> billing_cutback_fix

=== billing_cutback_fix ===
Billing traffic is cut back to the monolith while the team fixes the regression.
# critical-path
~ billing_cutbacks += 1
~ respin_budget -= 1
+ {billing_cutbacks < 3} [Fixed, re-run shadow parity] ~loop~ -> billing_shadow
+ {billing_cutbacks >= 3} [Third cutback, billing approach goes to the architecture board] @human -> arch_board_review

=== monolith_freeze_booking ===
Agree a change-freeze window with support for the monolith lift-and-shift.
If the window gets pulled later, we come back here and rebook, as many times as it takes.
# jira: SUP-77
~ freeze_window = "booked"
+ [Freeze window agreed and booked] -> monolith_capacity_signoff

=== monolith_capacity_signoff ===
Platform SRE reviews capacity for moving the remaining monolith onto the PaaS as-is.
+ [SRE signs off capacity] @human -> monolith_migration
+ [SRE flags gaps, remediate and rebook the window] @human ~loop~ -> monolith_freeze_booking

=== monolith_migration ===
Lift-and-shift the remaining monolith onto the PaaS during the agreed freeze window.
# linear: PLAT-590
+ [Freeze window pulled by support, rebook it] ~loop~ -> monolith_freeze_booking
+ [Monolith live on the PaaS] -> program_review

=== arch_board_review ===
The architecture board reviews the failing service's extraction approach after its third cutback.
The board either approves a revised approach for another attempt or halts the programme.
+ [Board approves a revised auth approach, restart that extraction] @human ~loop~ -> auth_extraction
+ [Board approves a revised billing approach, restart that extraction] @human ~loop~ -> billing_extraction
+ [Board halts the programme] @human -> END

=== program_review ===
End-of-programme review of the old estate.
Decide whether to decommission immediately or keep it warm for a quarter as insurance.
# report: at-end
* [Decommission the old estate] @human -> decommission
* [Keep the old estate warm for a quarter] @human -> keep_warm

=== keep_warm ===
The old estate stays warm for one quarter as insurance while the PaaS beds in.
* [Insurance quarter elapsed, decommission the old estate] @human -> decommission

=== decommission ===
Tear down the old estate: DNS records, data exports, hardware returns, licence cancellations.
-> END
